The [[Snowmaster]] is a [[Ranger]] [[Pet]] normally obtained by combining a [[Carrot]], a [[Snowball]], and a [[Lump of Coal]]. The [[Carrot]] needs to be the one touching both other items for the craft, despite how making a snowman would work in real life. The [[Snowmaster]] could also appear in the shop for [[Pyromancer]]s with the [[Frozen Flame]] or any class with the [[Speak with Animals]] [[Skill]].

The [[Snowmaster]] triggers quickly, inflicting a {{icon/cold}} to the enemy and cleansing a debuff with each activation. If the opponent has at least 10 {{icon/cold}}, {{icon/empower}} is gained instead of inflicting any more {{icon/cold}}.

It triggers faster for each {{icon/ice}} item near its base, up to a maximum of 50% faster.

Ice builds will certainly enjoy the [[Snowmaster]], as it does have a powerful effect, and the ability to inflict {{icon/cold}}, but as it can't inflict any {{icon/cold}} above 10, it's not particularly good for stacking high amounts of it, which is what one would want with something like the [[Frostbite]]. That said, mass amounts of {{icon/empower}} is generally not something that is gained easily, usually requiring jumping through some hoops, and as far as hoops go, 10 {{icon/cold}} can be pretty doable with the right supporting items, like maybe whatever can be crafted with the other [[Snowball]] from the [[Wonky Snowman]] purchased. If the {{icon/empower}} gain can be turned online early in the fight, and multiple [[Weapon]]s are used, this can go from a decent debuff source to a significant source of direct damage.

[[Snowmaster]] is one of the fastest-triggering items in the game, making it great with [[Goobert]]s and a few other items that count item triggers.
